From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] whyred: report block bytes through XNU d_psize

XNU8796 specfs set_blocksize uses d_psize as bytes per device block, not
partition capacity. Returning sector count makes a32MiB persist partition
appear to have65536-byte blocks, so spec_read rejects it above PAGE_SIZE.
Small partitions also get incorrect addressing units. Return the fixed512-byte
sector size; retain actual capacity in DKIOCGETBLOCKCOUNT. Write opens and
strategy writes remain denied. No user-space SETBLOCKSIZE policy change.

--- a/bsd/dev/whyred_emmc_pio_probe.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/whyred_emmc_pio_probe.c
@@ -1064,7 +1064,8 @@
 whyred_emmc_psize(dev_t dev)
 {
 	const struct whyred_gpt_partition *part = whyred_emmc_partition(dev);
-	return part == NULL ? -1 : (int)MIN(part->last - part->first + 1, INT_MAX);
+	/* XNU specfs uses d_psize for block bytes; capacity is a separate ioctl. */
+	return part == NULL ? -1 : WHYRED_GPT_BLOCK_BYTES;
 }
 
 static const struct bdevsw whyred_emmc_bdevsw = {
